# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Zolto (zolto.ch) — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in all values before running docker compose.
#
# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ THE GOLDEN RULE: env vars are for ZOLTO's (the platform's) credentials  │
# │ ONLY. Tenant credentials never live here.                               │
# │                                                                         │
# │   Platform (here, env):  Zolto's own Stripe account, the one platform   │
# │     Discord bot, DB password, encryption keys, S3, LLM, backups.        │
# │   Tenant (database, NEVER env):                                         │
# │     - Stripe: tenants link their OWN account via Stripe Connect OAuth   │
# │       (tenants.stripe_connected_account_id — an ID, not a secret).      │
# │     - POS API keys: generated per tenant, stored only as a SHA-256      │
# │       hash (tenants.pos_api_key); plaintext shown once at generation.   │
# │     - Discord: per-tenant channel/user IDs in tenant_settings (IDs,     │
# │       not secrets); the single platform bot below serves every tenant.  │
# │     - Any future tenant-provided token: the encrypted tenant_secrets    │
# │       vault (TENANT_SECRETS_KEY below + server/tenantSecrets.ts).       │
# │ Zolto admin can never read a tenant's credentials: nothing stores them  │
# │ in a retrievable form, and no endpoint returns them.                    │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# Standing up a SECOND instance on a server that already runs one (e.g. this
# repo alongside Kalakosh-ch)? Don't copy that instance's real .env wholesale.
# The database is safe either way — docker-compose gives each project its own
# isolated MySQL container/volume/network regardless of what credentials you
# put in here. But Stripe, S3, Discord, and Google OAuth are real external
# services with no such isolation — reusing another deployment's live values
# for those means test traffic hits its real payments/bucket/bot/login. Vars
# below that need a genuinely distinct value for a second instance are marked
# ⚠️ SEPARATE INSTANCE.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Isolated from the Kalakosh-ch stack (separate container + volume), but use
# distinct credentials anyway so nothing ever cross-connects by accident.
MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=change_me_root_password
MYSQL_DATABASE=zolto
MYSQL_USER=zolto_user
MYSQL_PASSWORD=change_me_db_password

# ── Session ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# ⚠️ SEPARATE INSTANCE: generate a fresh one per deployment — no reason to
# share the value that signs another instance's session cookies.
JWT_SECRET=a_long_random_string_at_least_32_chars

# ── Tenant secrets vault (master encryption key) ─────────────────────────────
# Encrypts every tenant-provided secret before it touches the database
# (tenant_secrets table, server/tenantSecrets.ts). Without it the vault is
# disabled; tenant features that need stored secrets will refuse to save them.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# ⚠️ SEPARATE INSTANCE: always a fresh key per deployment — sharing it would
# let one instance decrypt another instance's tenant_secrets backups.
# ⚠️ Losing this key makes all stored tenant secrets unrecoverable — back it
# up like the database password.
TENANT_SECRETS_KEY=

# ── Google OAuth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials
# 2. Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application)
# 3. Add Authorized redirect URI: https://zolto.ch/api/oauth/callback
# 4. Copy Client ID and Client Secret below
# ⚠️ SEPARATE INSTANCE: reusing another deployment's OAuth client will likely
# fail login outright — its Authorized redirect URIs won't include this
# instance's own address/port. Add that redirect URI to the existing client,
# or create a separate OAuth client for this instance.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_google_client_secret

# The only Google account allowed to log in as admin
ADMIN_EMAIL=shwena9@gmail.com

# ── Discord Bot (platform bot — one bot serves ALL tenants) ─────────────────
# This is Zolto's own bot; tenants never provide a token. A tenant invites
# this bot to their Discord server and registers their channel/user IDs in
# their store settings (tenant_settings.discord_channel_id /
# discord_owner_user_id, editable via the admin UI). Those IDs are not
# secrets and live in the database, not here.
#
# Bot token from discord.com/developers/applications → Bot → Token
# ⚠️ SEPARATE INSTANCE: reusing another deployment's bot/channel/user ID means
# product intake and "new order" DMs from this instance land in that
# deployment's real Discord channel/DMs. Use a separate bot application (and
# channel) for a second instance, or leave these blank if you're not testing
# that flow right now — notifications just log to the console instead.
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=Bot_token_here

# LEGACY fallback only: channel to watch when no tenant has a channel mapping
# (single-tenant self-hosted). Multi-tenant routing uses
# tenant_settings.discord_channel_id instead.
DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID=

# Platform-owner Discord user ID — fallback DM recipient when a tenant hasn't
# set their own (tenant_settings.discord_owner_user_id).
# Right-click your own name in Discord → Copy User ID (Developer Mode must be
# on). Optional — if not set, notifications log to the server console instead.
DISCORD_OWNER_USER_ID=

# ── Stripe Payments (platform account) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Zolto's OWN Stripe account. Two distinct jobs run on it:
#   1. Platform billing — charging MERCHANTS for their plan + AI photo credits
#      (STRIPE_PRICE_* below).
#   2. Connect platform — creating charges/Terminal PaymentIntents ON a
#      tenant's connected account via the stripeAccount parameter.
# Tenants' storefront money NEVER touches this account: each tenant links
# their own Stripe account via Stripe Connect OAuth (server/stripeConnect.ts)
# and their customers pay them directly. You only ever store their
# acct_... ID — never their API keys.
#
# Setup:
# 1. Create a Stripe account (use a Swiss/CHF account so TWINT is available).
# 2. Dashboard → Developers → API keys → copy the Secret key below.
# 3. Dashboard → Payments → enable "TWINT" and "Cards" payment methods.
# 4. Dashboard → Developers → Webhooks → add endpoint
#    https://zolto.ch/api/stripe/webhook and subscribe to
#    checkout.session.completed, checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded,
#    checkout.session.async_payment_failed, checkout.session.expired
#    then copy the "Signing secret" into STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
# If STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is left blank, checkout falls back to WhatsApp enquiry.
# ⚠️ SEPARATE INSTANCE: use a TEST-mode key (sk_test_...) here, not another
# deployment's live key (sk_live_...) — a shared live key means anything you
# do while testing this instance (checkout, refunds) hits real payments.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_your_stripe_secret_key
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_your_webhook_signing_secret

# ── Stripe Connect (tenants link their own Stripe accounts) ──────────────────
# The platform's Connect OAuth client id (ca_...), from Dashboard → Connect →
# Settings. This is the platform's own identifier — tenants authenticate on
# Stripe's pages and Zolto only ever receives their connected account id.
# If unset, "connect your Stripe account" is disabled for tenants.
STRIPE_CONNECT_CLIENT_ID=

# ── Platform Billing (Zolto charging merchants for plans + AI photo credits) ───
# These Price ids belong to Zolto's own Stripe account and bill the MERCHANT.
# Create three recurring Prices matching shared/platform.ts
# (Maker CHF 19/mo, Studio CHF 49/mo, Atelier CHF 99/mo) and one one-time
# CHF 1 Price for AI photo credits. Webhook: also subscribe the platform
# endpoint above to customer.subscription.created / .updated / .deleted and
# invoice.payment_succeeded so plan state and monthly credit buckets sync.
# If unset, paid-plan checkout is disabled (free signup still works).
STRIPE_PRICE_MAKER=
STRIPE_PRICE_STUDIO=
STRIPE_PRICE_ATELIER=
STRIPE_PRICE_PHOTO_CREDIT=

# ── Stripe Test Keys (for integration tests) ──────────────────────────────────────
# These are used by `pnpm test:integration` to run real API tests against
# Stripe's test environment. They should match your STRIPE_SECRET_KEY and
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET above if you're using test keys. In CI, set these
# as GitHub repository secrets (Settings → Secrets → Actions).
# Integration tests auto-skip if these are unset.
STRIPE_TEST_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_TEST_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Canonical site URL used for Stripe success/cancel redirects.
# Leave blank to derive it from the incoming request origin.
# ⚠️ SEPARATE INSTANCE: must point at THIS instance's own reachable address,
# not another deployment's domain — otherwise a completed checkout redirects
# the customer to the wrong site.
# When running alongside Kalakosh-ch (served at zolto.ch via the Kalakosh-ch
# Caddy over the shared network), set this to https://zolto.ch so Stripe
# redirects and absolute URLs are correct.
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://zolto.ch

# ── Docker Compose: Caddy (docker-compose.yml) ─────────────────────────────────
#
# RECOMMENDED — run alongside the Kalakosh-ch stack and serve Zolto at
# zolto.ch. In this mode Zolto does NOT run its own Caddy or bind any
# host ports; the Kalakosh-ch Caddy (on 80/443) reverse-proxies zolto.ch
# to Zolto's app over the shared "kalakosh-shared" Docker network. The three
# variables below are unused in this mode — just:
#   1. docker network create kalakosh-shared        # once, if not already made
#   2. add DNS A records: zolto.ch and www.zolto.ch -> server IP
#   3. in the Kalakosh-ch Caddyfile, add:
#        zolto.ch { reverse_proxy zolto-app:3000 }
#        www.zolto.ch { redir https://zolto.ch{uri} permanent }
#   4. docker compose up -d                          # no bundled Caddy starts
#
# STANDALONE — run Zolto with its bundled Caddy via
#   docker compose --profile standalone up -d
# (Only when nothing else owns 80/443, or remap HTTP_PORT/HTTPS_PORT below.)
# The settings below apply only in that standalone mode:
#
# SITE_DOMAIN: "zolto.ch" (default) — Caddy auto-provisions HTTPS for it and
# redirects www.zolto.ch to the apex. Set ":80" for plain-HTTP testing against
# the server's IP before DNS is pointed over.
SITE_DOMAIN=zolto.ch
# Host ports the standalone Caddy binds. Defaults deliberately avoid 80/443 so
# this stack can also coexist with another instance on its own ports.
HTTP_PORT=8080
HTTPS_PORT=8443

# ── POS Terminal (Tap to Pay for market stall sales) ───────────────────────────
# THERE IS NO POS_API_KEY ENV VAR. POS keys are per-tenant: generated at
# signup / rotated from the tenant's admin panel (tenant.rotatePosApiKey),
# stored only as a SHA-256 hash (tenants.pos_api_key), and shown to the
# tenant exactly once. The tenant enters it into their POS app, which sends
# it as the X-POS-Key header.
#
# Dashboard → Developers → Webhooks → add endpoint
#   https://zolto.ch/api/pos/webhook and subscribe to payment_intent.succeeded
#   then copy the "Signing secret" here. (Platform account webhook — events
#   for tenants' connected accounts also arrive here via Connect.)
STRIPE_POS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# LEGACY fallback only: a Stripe Terminal Location on the PLATFORM account,
# served to POS apps of single-tenant self-hosted deployments that never
# connected their own account. Multi-tenant deployments create a Location per
# tenant on that tenant's Connect account on first use (tml_...).
STRIPE_LOCATION_ID=

# ── Transactional Email (Resend) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sends order receipt emails to customers after a successful payment.
# 1. Sign in at https://resend.com and verify the zolto.ch domain.
# 2. Create an API key and paste it below.
# 3. Set RESEND_FROM_EMAIL to a verified sender address on the zolto.ch domain.
# If RESEND_API_KEY is left blank, receipt emails are silently skipped.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_your_resend_api_key
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=Zolto <orders@zolto.ch>

# ── LLM — OpenAI-compatible API ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Option A: Groq (fast, generous free tier — recommended)
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=gsk_...
# LLM_MODEL=llama3-8b-8192

# Option B: OpenAI
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Option C: Ollama (fully local, free — must be accessible from the container)
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=ollama
# LLM_MODEL=llama3

LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
LLM_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key
LLM_MODEL=llama3-8b-8192

# ── S3-compatible Storage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Option A: Cloudflare R2 (recommended — free 10 GB, no egress fees)
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://<account_id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# S3_REGION=auto
# S3_PUBLIC_URL=https://pub-<hash>.r2.dev   ← enable public access in R2 dashboard

# Option B: AWS S3
# S3_ENDPOINT=   ← leave blank for AWS
# S3_REGION=eu-central-1
# S3_PUBLIC_URL=  ← leave blank to use signed URL proxy

# Option C: Backblaze B2
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.us-west-004.backblazeb2.com
# S3_REGION=us-west-004
# S3_PUBLIC_URL=https://f004.backblazeb2.com/file/<bucket>

# ⚠️ SEPARATE INSTANCE: point at a genuinely separate bucket (new bucket + new
# scoped access key) for a second instance — reusing another deployment's
# bucket/keys writes test images straight into its real, live bucket.
S3_BUCKET=zolto-images
S3_REGION=auto
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_access_key
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_secret_key
S3_ENDPOINT=https://your_account_id.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# Leave blank to serve via signed URL proxy (/uploads/* route)
S3_PUBLIC_URL=

# ── Backup: secondary S3 (redundancy) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Point at a DIFFERENT provider from the primary above (e.g. Backblaze B2 if
# primary is Cloudflare R2). deploy/backup.sh uploads to both — if one goes
# down the other still has your backup. Leave blank to skip.
BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=zolto-backups
BACKUP_S3_REGION=us-west-004
BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_b2_key_id
BACKUP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_b2_app_key
BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.us-west-004.backblazeb2.com

# ── Backup: GitHub private repository ────────────────────────────────────────
# Each weekly backup is committed as backup.sql + inventory.csv to this repo.
# Git history lets you diff any two weeks to see exactly what stock changed.
# Setup:
#   1. Create a private repo (e.g. youruser/zolto-backups)
#   2. Generate a fine-grained PAT: Settings → Developer settings →
#      Fine-grained tokens → Contents: Read and Write for that repo only
# Leave blank to skip.
BACKUP_GITHUB_REPO=youruser/zolto-backups
BACKUP_GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_...

# Public hostname of the platform itself — shown to tenants as the CNAME
# target for their custom domains and used by the DNS status check.
PLATFORM_DOMAIN=zolto.ch
